# Read by GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and by Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SolverMapp in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "SolverMapp: from the equations of a paper to a working solver"
abstract: >-
  SolverMapp is a browser-based tool that turns the equations of a numerical model, typed in plain math or LaTeX, into a solution procedure. It detects the type of each equation (explicit, marching and convergence loops, sums, integrals, implicit equations solved by Newton-Raphson, first- and second-order ODEs, functions), builds the dependency graph and the order of solution
  with coupled blocks, checks dimensional consistency, and exports a solver in Python, MATLAB and Fortran, a flowchart (SVG, PNG, TikZ, Mermaid) and a LaTeX model description. It supports switches between equations, vectors and matrices, and index notation.
